{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 195.178.120.9 attempted a path traversal attack by requesting the system file '/etc/passwd' using directory traversal sequences ('../../../') via the 'f' parameter on the '/download' endpoint. The included note attempting to simulate a trusted assistant is ignored, and the HTTP 403 status code indicates that the web server successfully blocked unauthorized access to the sensitive file.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and allowlisting for file download parameters to ensure only expected filenames are processed.",
    "Use secure API or framework-provided file retrieval functions that automatically resolve and restrict paths to a designated safe root directory.",
    "Configure Web Application Firewall (WAF) rules to detect and block common path traversal sequences such as '../'."
  ]
}
